---
import CTAButton from "../CTAButton.astro";

const mistakes = [
  "Ordering a QoE report before terms are agreed. $8,000 to $15,000 gone in week two.",
  "Paying an M&A attorney to draft an LOI a template would cover. $2,000 to $4,000.",
  "Running QoE and legal review at the same time. The deal dies on the numbers after $6,000 in legal bills.",
  "Picking the wrong lender and finding out in month three.",
  "Skipping the $500 lien search and paying for it at closing.",
  "Overpaying by half a turn because nobody told you what it should trade for. On a $1.5M deal, that's $75,000.",
];
---

<section class="py-16 md:py-24">
  <div class="fade-in-section mx-auto max-w-[1100px] px-4 sm:px-6">
    <h2
      class="max-w-3xl font-serif text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-4xl"
    >
      Most first-time buyers don't lose money on the price. They lose it on the
      order of operations.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft">
      I see these every month. All of them are avoidable.
    </p>

    <ul class="mt-10 flex max-w-[46rem] flex-col divide-y divide-line">
      {
        mistakes.map((mistake) => (
          <li class="py-5 leading-relaxed text-ink">{mistake}</li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-10 max-w-prose text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      Your CPA, attorney, QoE firm, and lender are all necessary. None of them
      is paid to tell you what order to go in, or when to stop. That's my job.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 max-w-md border-l-2 border-accent bg-white/60 py-6 pl-6 pr-6">
      <p class="text-base text-ink">Six months of Quarterback: $3,000</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-base text-ink">Under Contract: $2,500</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-base text-ink">
        One QoE report on a deal that was going to die anyway: $10,000
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <CTAButton offering="dealCall" label="Book a Deal Call" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
